{"schemaVersion":1,"slug":"jump-game-ii","title":"Jump Game II","pattern":"Greedy","difficulty":"Medium","leetcode":45,"prompt":"The last index is always reachable. Return the fewest jumps needed to get there from index 0.","examples":[{"input":"nums = [2,3,1,1,4]","output":"2","why":"Jump to index 1, then to the end."},{"input":"nums = [2,3,0,1,4]","output":"2"}],"constraints":["1 <= len(nums) <= 10^4","The end is always reachable"],"approaches":[{"id":"table","label":"Fewest jumps to every index","complexity":{"time":"O(n\u00b7max)","space":"O(n)"},"viz":{"nums":"array","best":"array","i":"pointer:nums","j":"pointer:best"},"layout":{},"source":["def dp_table(nums):","    best = [BIG] * len(nums)","    best[0] = 0","    for i in range(len(nums)):","        for step in range(1, nums[i] + 1):","            j = i + step","            if j < len(nums) and best[i] + 1 < best[j]:","                best[j] = best[i] + 1","    return best[len(nums) - 1]"],"variants":[{"id":"typical","label":"Typical","note":null,"result":2,"steps":[{"line":0,"ops":[["set",["nums"],[2,3,1,1,4]]],"note":null},{"line":1,"ops":[["set",["best"],[1000000000,1000000000,1000000000,1000000000,1000000000]]],"note":"for every position rather than only the last one."},{"line":2,"ops":[["set",["best",0],0]],"note":null},{"line":3,"ops":[["set",["i"],0]],"note":null},{"line":4,"ops":[["set",["step"],1]],"note":null},{"line":5,"ops":[["set",["j"],1]],"note":null},{"line":6,"ops":[],"note":"Reaching j via i costs one more jump than reaching i did."},{"line":7,"ops":[["set",["best",1],1]],"note":null},{"line":4,"ops":[["set",["step"],2]],"note":null},{"line":5,"ops":[["set",["j"],2]],"note":null},{"line":6,"ops":[],"note":"Reaching j via i costs one more jump than reaching i did."},{"line":7,"ops":[["set",["best",2],1]],"note":null},{"line":4,"ops":[],"note":null},{"line":3,"ops":[["set",["i"],1]],"note":null},{"line":4,"ops":[["set",["step"],1]],"note":null},{"line":5,"ops":[],"note":null},{"line":6,"ops"